      "content": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstdlib>\n#include <climits>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nstatic const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\nstatic char buf[BUFSIZE];\nstatic int pos = 0, len = 0;\n\ninline char getChar() {\n    if (pos >= len) {\n        len = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n        pos = 0;\n    }\n    return buf[pos++];\n}\n\ninline int readInt() {\n    char c;\n    do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\n    int sign = 1;\n    if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\n    int x = c - '0';\n    for (;;) {\n        c = getChar();\n        if (c < '0' || c > '9') break;\n        x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n    }\n    return sign * x;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = readInt();\n    int s = readInt();\n\n    const size_t N = static_cast<size_t>(n) + 1;\n    void* mem = nullptr;\n    if (posix_memalign(&mem, 64, sizeof(long long) * N * N) != 0) return 1;\n    long long* P = static_cast<long long*>(mem);\n\n    // Initialize first row and column to zero.\n    for (size_t j = 0; j < N; ++j) P[j] = 0;\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < N; ++i) P[i * N] = 0;\n\n    // Read matrix and compute 2D prefix sums.\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        const size_t curRow = static_cast<size_t>(i + 1) * N;\n        const size_t prevRow = static_cast<size_t>(i) * N;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int val = readInt();\n            P[curRow + j + 1] = static_cast<long long>(val)\n                              + P[prevRow + j + 1]\n                              + P[curRow + j]\n                              - P[prevRow + j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    const int limit_i = n - s;\n    const int limit_j = n - s;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= limit_i; ++i) {\n        const long long* base1 = &P[static_cast<size_t>(i) * N];\n        const long long* base2 = &P[static_cast<size_t>(i + s) * N];\n        long long rowBest = LLONG_MIN;\n        #pragma omp simd reduction(max:rowBest)\n        for (int j = 0; j <= limit_j; ++j) {\n            long long sum = base2[j + s] - base1[j + s] - base2[j] + base1[j];\n            if (sum > rowBest) rowBest = sum;\n        }\n        mxSum = std::max(mxSum, rowBest);\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n\n    free(mem);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Integrating A's fast fread-based scanner and aligned allocation, B's 2D prefix sums with OpenMP parallel-for reduction over starting rows and SIMD inner loops, and C's use of static scheduling yields a correct solution that minimizes I/O overhead while exploiting multi-core parallelism and vectorized window-sum computation.",
  "notes": "The implementation uses long long for prefix sums to avoid overflow. The first row/column are zero-initialized; the rest is filled during input reading. OpenMP pragmas enable parallel execution on the available cores, and SIMD reduction accelerates the inner loop. All valid inputs remain correct because the algorithm computes exact window sums.",
